MLOps Interview Series Part 3

1️⃣ What are the key components of an end-to-end MLOps pipeline?
Data ingestion & preprocessing → Experiment tracking (MLflow/SageMaker Experiments) → Model training (batch/distributed) → Model registry → CI/CD/CT pipelines → Model deployment (REST endpoints) → Model monitoring (latency, drift, data quality) → Automated retraining → Governance/logging

2️⃣ How do you detect data drift and model drift in production?
Data Drift: Statistical tests (KS test, PSI, Jensen-Shannon divergence) 
Model Drift: Monitor prediction distribution, accuracy drop, confidence score shifts 
Tools: SageMaker Model Monitor, Evidently AI, Fiddler, WhyLabs, custom Airflow jobs
3️⃣ How do you implement CI/CD for ML using GitHub Actions or CodePipeline?
CI: Lint → Unit tests → Data validation → Model training on branch 
CD: Register model → Deploy to staging → Smoke tests → Promote to prod GitHub Actions triggers training, Docker build, ECR/EKS deployment. CodePipeline integrates with Lambda/Step Functions for approvals.

4️⃣ What's the difference between MLflow and Kubeflow?
MLflow: Lightweight tool for experiment tracking, model registry, packaging, deployment 
Kubeflow: Full ML platform on Kubernetes with training operators, pipelines, Katib (HPO) 

5️⃣ How do SageMaker endpoints scale for inference?
Auto-scaling based on CPU, RAM, or custom metrics Multi-model endpoints (many models on one container) Serverless inference for spiky traffic (scales 0-200 invocations)

6️⃣ What is feature drift and how do you monitor it?
Feature drift = input features change distribution over time 
Monitor by: Store baseline feature stats → Compare live data with Evidently AI, SageMaker DataQuality Monitor → Trigger alerts via CloudWatch/Prometheus

7️⃣ How would you deploy and monitor a FastAPI ML model on Kubernetes?
Deploy: Containerize FastAPI → Push to ECR → Deploy via Helm with Deployment, Service, HPA, Ingress/ALB 
Monitor: Prometheus/Grafana for metrics, OpenTelemetry traces, ELK/Loki logs

8️⃣ Explain experiment tracking and why it's important.
Records parameters, metrics, artifacts, code versions, environment dependencies 
Tools: MLflow, SageMaker Experiments, Weights & Biases Enables reproducibility, model comparison, auditability, CI/CD integration.

9️⃣ How do you automate retraining pipelines?
Triggers: Data drift, model drift, scheduled retraining 
Using: Airflow DAGs, Kubeflow Pipelines, SageMaker Pipelines
 Steps: Fetch data → validate → train → evaluate → register → deploy

🔟 What is the recommended architecture for MLOps on AWS?

Data: S3 data lake, Glue/Athena/Lambda
 preprocessing Training: SageMaker Training + HPO, Model Registry 
Deploy: SageMaker Endpoints, ECR + EKS/ECS 
Monitor: CloudWatch + Model Monitor Orchestration: Step Functions 
